{"request_id":2,"ok":true,"result":{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"execute_python","description":"Execute ordinary persistent Python with stdout/stderr over CAPTURE_REPLAY inputs. geometry={'objects':[{'name':str,'vertices':[[rational_x,rational_y,rational_z],...],'triangles':[[i,j,k],...]}]} and cameras={'views':[{'name':str,'view_matrix':4x4,'projection_matrix':4x4,'direction_rational':[x,y,z],'size_px':[512,512],...}],...} reside in Python. np and Fraction are available. Raw inputs are returned only when requested or printed. render_views(names,include_images=False,fresh=False) returns current bound frames or constructs missing ones. fresh=True constructs one new frame per distinct requested view; repeated names within one call reuse that frame. buffers[ref] is a stable frame handle; buffers[view] is the latest alias. They contain color uint8[H,W,3], depth float64[H,W], owners int32[H,W] and triangle_ids int32[H,W]. Pixel origin is top-left, indices zero-based. owners identifies geometry.objects; triangle_ids is the global source-face index in object/face input order. Both owners use -1 for background; background depth is infinity. Base material RGB is (180,190,205). rendered RGB retains the common geometry-based shading. Merge source triangle IDs into your own target surface before boundary/readability calculations. Count unique target-owned pixels incident to horizontal/vertical different-surface pairs with RGB distance at least 24, marking both endpoints. read_images(refs) or attach_images(refs) appends actual generated images to this result; render_views(...,include_images=True) combines generation and image delivery. Product frames with verified raw triangle IDs enter the same buffers table. Legacy frames missing raw IDs cause an explicit capability miss and one native construction on first render_views access. Existing buffers and image refs can be reused directly. scratch is a writable Path, image_files maps refs to generated PNG paths. Use ordinary Python/NumPy/Fraction and your own algorithms. Product discovery, visibility-index, selection and location aggregation APIs are outside this common tool. Keep source inputs unchanged.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"code":{"type":"string"}},"required":["code"],"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"scene_data","description":"Read complete raw CAPTURE_REPLAY world geometry and candidate camera parameters. The same objects are already in execute_python variables geometry and cameras.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"render_views","description":"Read or generate full-scene views using the shared exact inputs and common RGB/depth/owner renderer. Default fresh=false reuses complete source/camera/owner-bound frames, including current product frames carrying verified raw triangle IDs. fresh=true constructs once per distinct requested view. Return stable refs and raw buffer handles; old refs retain their original arrays after fresh. include_images requests actual image content in this result.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"names":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":6,"items":{"type":"string","enum":["SCENE","TOP","LEFT","RIGHT","FRONT","BACK"]}},"include_images":{"type":"boolean","default":false},"fresh":{"type":"boolean","default":false}},"required":["names"],"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"read_images","description":"Return actual 512x512 PNG image content for one or multiple generated current-session image refs. Input order is retained. The source views reuse their render cache.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"refs":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":6,"items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["refs"],"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"active_observation","description":"Use the current installed engine on CAPTURE_REPLAY through its normal read-only observation service. Returns its default source-bound brief-v4 region locations, actual pixel facts, image references and remaining unknowns. include_images=true performs observation with native images. False uses the product's prediction-only text mode. Repeated requests use the same slot's normal product cache. Complete frames with raw triangle IDs are registered for default render_views reuse. After successful delivery, json.loads(last_observation_json) in execute_python reads this same public JSON text.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"include_images":{"type":"boolean","default":true}},"additionalProperties":false}}]}}}
